**Closed, with the lines they rest on**
- Picking the folder the workspace already points at in "Change folder…" returns an `unchanged` result, and the renderer skips the toast (`apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/relocate.ts:43`) — No toast and no window prompt. The dialog's `onRelocated` call (workspace-dialog.tsx:145) and Settings' `changeFolder` (workspaces-context.tsx:184-185) both go through the same `onRelocated`, so both stay silent. If it fails: The path comparison uses `resolve()` and is case-sensitive. On a case-insensitive macOS volume, picking the same folder with different casing misses the early return and runs the full transaction, wh… Evidence: `apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/relocate.ts:37-48`, `apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/index.ts:340-350`, `apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspaces-context.tsx:165-192`, `apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspace-dialog.tsx:144-146`.
- An offline edit of a `pendingInit` workspace now keeps `pendingInit` (`apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:634`) — Renaming while the drive is away no longer makes "Change folder…" refuse the moved folder. The registry-relocate test covers this path. If it fails: The edit's own failure paths are unchanged: a failed identity write returns `not-writable`, and a failed registry update rolls the folder back. Evidence: `apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:603-650`, `apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry-relocate.test.ts:221-243`.

